[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4480348152","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/119552#issuecomment-4480348152","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/119552","id":4480348152,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABCwyv-A","user":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-05-18T17:51:29Z","updated_at":"2026-05-18T17:59:23Z","body":"In general (as documented) values have to be written to in all paths, and also a lot of shader features trigger special behavior if referenced, the shader compiler doesn't do static analysis and enables certain features for the entire shader if they are used\n\nI'd suggest using defines instead to control conditional behavior like this, or just write an appropriate value to it otherwise\n\nNote that the default is declared here:\nhttps://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/ef02314f2bd0305035ecbe907883401a393da7a7/servers/rendering/renderer_rd/shaders/forward_clustered/scene_forward_clustered.glsl#L1298-L1300\nhttps://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/ef02314f2bd0305035ecbe907883401a393da7a7/drivers/gles3/shaders/scene.glsl#L2277-L2279","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4480348152/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4481411183","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/119552#issuecomment-4481411183","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/119552","id":4481411183,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABCxzobw","user":{"login":"dhoverb","id":226178021,"node_id":"U_kgDODXsz5Q","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/226178021?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dhoverb","html_url":"https://github.com/dhoverb","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dhoverb/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dhoverb/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dhoverb/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dhoverb/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dhoverb/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dhoverb/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dhoverb/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dhoverb/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dhoverb/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-05-18T19:46:21Z","updated_at":"2026-05-18T19:46:21Z","body":"> In general (as documented) values have to be written to in all paths, and also a lot of shader features trigger special behavior if referenced\n\nI suspected this.  Do you know where it is documented?\n\nI also couldn't find documentation on how to define/undefine ifdefs at runtime (I am looking at this https://docs.godotengine.org/en/4.4/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/shader_preprocessor.html)\n\nFor example, if the shader has this (and no `#define USE_ALPHA_SHADER` anywhere else)\n```\n  #ifdef USE_ALPHA_SHADER\n    ALPHA_SCISSOR_THRESHOLD = 0.2;\n  #endf\n```\nis there a function to define it and recompile the shader? like:\n```gdscript\nmy_shader_material.set_shader_define(\"USE_ALPHA_SHADER\") # adds \"#define USE_ALPHA_SHADER\" to the shader and recompiles it\n```\nOtherwise I could add some code to generate the shader code (which is doable, just not ideal).  I'm trying to avoid duplicating a shader to change one line of code.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4481411183/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4486505408","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/119552#issuecomment-4486505408","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/119552","id":4486505408,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABC2qjwA","user":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-05-19T09:45:50Z","updated_at":"2026-05-19T10:01:44Z","body":"Don't remember where exactly now, might have misremembered\n\nFor using defines, I didn't realize that they can't be directly used with normal materials, my bad, haven't used the functionality\n\nSo in that case I'd say the variable should be written to in an `else` block, unfortunately\n\nThe default value of this should probably be documented as it is surprising, and perhaps a note about writing to it in all code paths","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4486505408/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4492441287","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/119552#issuecomment-4492441287","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/119552","id":4492441287,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABC8U2xw","user":{"login":"Calinou","id":180032,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MDAzMg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/180032?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou","html_url":"https://github.com/Calinou","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-05-19T22:05:26Z","updated_at":"2026-05-19T22:06:37Z","body":"Any of the \"If written to\" built-ins will have an effect as soon as you write to them on *any* branch, even one that is `if (false)`. When written to, they have a fallback value that is used and doesn't always make sense, but we should avoid changing it to keep compatibility with existing shaders.\n\n> I also couldn't find documentation on how to define/undefine ifdefs at runtime\n\nThis isn't possible yet:\n\n- https://github.com/godotengine/godot-proposals/issues/8076","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4492441287/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]